ADS-001 — Purpose & Scope

Document ID: ADS-001
Title: Purpose & Scope
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification establishes the Atlas Data Specification (ADS) as the canonical standard governing the structure, semantics, lifecycle, governance, and interoperability of all data managed within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

ADS transforms the architectural concepts defined by ACC and AHS into formal data specifications that can be implemented consistently across platforms, services, and deployment environments.

2. Objectives

ADS SHALL:

Define canonical data objects.
Define canonical schemas.
Define metadata standards.
Define relationships between objects.
Define versioning rules.
Define serialization independence.
Define validation requirements.
Define interoperability requirements.
3. Scope

ADS governs:

Canonical Atlas Objects (CAO)
Canonical Engineering Artifacts (CEA)
Decision Records (DR)
Canonical Events (CEV)
Canonical Communication Envelopes (CCE)
Canonical Interface Contracts (CIC)
Canonical Trust Objects (CTO)
Metadata
Relationships
Versioning
Validation
Identifiers
Data lifecycle

ADS does not define:

Databases
SQL schemas
NoSQL collections
File formats
APIs
Programming language classes

Those belong to implementation profiles.

4. Relationship to Other Specifications

ADS SHALL conform to:

ACC
AHS

Future specifications SHALL reference ADS for all canonical data definitions.

ADS SHALL become the normative data standard for Atlas.

5. Design Principles

Atlas data SHALL be:

Semantic

Meaning SHALL be explicit.

Canonical

Every concept SHALL have one canonical representation.

Technology Independent

No implementation assumptions.

Traceable

Every object SHALL preserve provenance.

Explainable

Supporting evidence SHALL remain available.

Versioned

Every governed object SHALL support version history.

Extensible

Future domains SHALL extend existing definitions rather than replace them.

6. Canonical Data Families

ADS defines the following canonical families.

Canonical Atlas Object (CAO)
│
├── Canonical Engineering Artifact (CEA)
│
├── Decision Record (DR)
│
├── Canonical Event (CEV)
│
├── Communication Envelope (CCE)
│
├── Interface Contract (CIC)
│
├── Trust Object (CTO)
│
├── Workflow Object (CWO)
│
├── Policy Object (CPO)
│
└── Future Extensions

Every governed Atlas object SHALL belong to one of these families.

